#heading(level: 1, "Actual M31 relation-lead comparisons - 2026-11-27")
#text("This run implements and tests the proposed components themselves. The previous 56-cell native auxiliary-IC run was a baseline only and did not evaluate these changes. Both historical runs remain separate. The coordinate field is Fp, p=2147483647=2^31-1; the curve is y^2=x^3+2x+14, N=2147505293, G=(1,814455902). [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#heading(level: 2, "Observed outcomes")
#text("All 146 planned native processes emitted reports: 120 polynomial encoding/schedule cells, 24 real collection cells and two target/cancellation controls. No process was excluded or killed. Native correctness tests passed 6/6; the deliberate failed transport call did not skip the next successful call. Extra native replay is validation, not a new comparison cell. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("On the four fixed planted cases, balanced S3, monolithic S4/S5 and partial S4/S3 each returned group-replayed witnesses under both schedules. Serial S3 returned witnesses on three cases under each schedule and hit its cap on k=4,m=4. Guarded explicit addition returned a witness only on k=2,m=3 under either schedule. These are bounded native F4 plus finite-domain substitution outcomes, not pure-F4 completion or an end-to-end IC speedup. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("The mixed-lift control numerically evaluates S5 to zero on x=(1,0,5,1650294539), target G. The implemented salvage procedure consumes supplied signed Fp2 lifts, classifies rational terms, and checks the doubled relation: four terms become one rational projected term. This constructed example has T=O, as expected for this odd-order curve; it does not test a nonzero rational 2-torsion contribution or establish salvage frequency. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("Actual sampled collection accepted four one/two-outside-point partials. Their outside coefficient matrices produced zero dependencies and zero combined final rows within the cap. Separate synthetic signed-cancellation controls returned 52 replayed nonidentity combined targets from 64 rows and outside rank12; these are excluded from generation yield. The all-positive triangle has rank3 modulo101 and was not accepted as a dependency. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#heading(level: 2, "Frozen design and accounting")
#text("Protocol/input/seed freeze: commit 4fff25b. Worker source: `91e9ea5c1ec0e604ad28dfdf12cf87f47b396eae`; encoding implementation a5c1354, native replay implementation 8006bf2. Exact binary hashes and all commands are in manifest.json. All solver input files contain public coordinates; no generating scalar reaches these workers. Native sampler/base seeds and bounded deterministic root splitting are frozen in seeds.json. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("Encoding panel: first k=2 or4 rational interval lifts, m=3 or4; one planted sum plus two ordinary targets per (k,m). Five encodings crossed with global/incremental-staged solving, grevlex degree cap8, one shared 2-s engine/recovery budget and a separate construction budget10s. Worker guard:20s/2GiB. Monolithic S4/S5 are actual Sylvester resultants; all encodings use common leaf-domain quotient reduction. Staging retains original equations and carries derived bases. Explicit addition has identity, inverse, doubling and distinct-x guarded branches, with canonical infinity coordinates and inactive slopes. [pcc:unverified]")
#parbreak()
#text("Collection panel: ambient71 signed columns and final53 columns, outside18, on torus, interval and ordinary random bases with equal column counts. The same direct decomposition backend isolates base selection. Each cell requests256 coefficient-walk targets with a5-s soft cap. Full and partial methods share identical native query streams and exact same bases; only a common completed prefix can support a paired comparison. Partial acceptance uses the first found witness and rejects witnesses with more than two outside terms; it does not prove another admissible witness is absent. [pcc:unverified]")
